Ctrl+F is find, and there is one conversation mode
==================================================

Ctrl+K for search is a shortcut for people who already know it. Ctrl+F is the one everybody reaches
for, because every program they have used since 1995 has used it for exactly this. Inside a
conversation Ctrl+F finds in that conversation; anywhere else it opens search, which is the same
instinct one level up. Ctrl+K still works — nothing that used to be true stops being true.

Settings had a Conversation block: a mode select and a push-to-talk key. The composer's Mic and
Speaker switches are that mode now, so it was two descriptions of one thing, and the second one could
only ever disagree with the first. Removed rather than hidden. Device choice, engines and voice stay
where they were.

